  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Refactored WikiView.vue component** to use new API-driven endpoints instead of file-based structure, mapping L0 (Home), L1 (Domains), L2 (Modules), and L3 (Files) navigation levels.\n\n2. **Integrated existing API methods** from `api.js` including `wiki.read()`, `wiki.index()`, `wiki.buildModulePage()`, and `files.read()` for seamless data retrieval.\n\n3. **Reorganized navigation flow** from previous category-based system to a streamlined domain-to-module hierarchy with breadcrumb tracking and active state management.\n\n4. **Enhanced UX with loading states** and error handling, displaying spinners during async operations and fallback messages when content unavailable.\n\n5. **Maintained component structure** with split-pane layout (sidebar + content area) while updating internal logic to fetch and display dynamic wiki index data from backend endpoints.",
